/* A cinema sells movie tickets for ₹X each. A customer buys Y tickets and has a total budget of ₹Z.
Write a C program to determine whether the customer can afford all the tickets and still have at least ₹100 left.*/

#include<stdio.h>
int main(){
    int x,y,z;
    scanf("%d %d %d", &x, &y, &z);
    if(z-(x*y) >=100)
        printf("yes");
    else
        printf("no");
    return 0;
}

sol:
x * y calculates the total ticket cost.
z - (x * y) calculates the remaining money.
>= 100 checks whether at least ₹100 remains.
